         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Images from Mi Pueblito\n\nThese images are copyright for Mi Pueblito and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 1</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgMiPueblito0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgMiPueblito0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Indigenous constructions in <i>Mi Pueblito</i>, Panama. Photo taken on <htdate0>, during a visit to the site (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Ages and Pyramids - what do a pyramid and the dates of our birthdays have in common? (<htcite1>)</li><li>Learning from nature - This text explores how knowledge of multiplication could have helped ancient civilizations. (<htcite2>)</li><li>The result is (Phase II) - a game to reinforce the connection between addition and multiplication. (<htcite3>)</li><li>Translation game (Part I) - Explore numbers from different cultures through an engaging translation game. (<htcite4>)</li><li>The result is - a game of consecutive sums that helps uncover the story. (<htcite5>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
